# Tooling

Summary: Shared tool conventions and the integration behavior of the enabled language workspaces. A project's `tools.md` defines its exact invocations and wins over these defaults.

## za

- `za` is the canonical command for managing this workspace's architecture.
- It replaces hand-written management scripts: never add shell, Python or Make scripts under `.agents/` that duplicate workspace-management behavior.
- Available: `za init`, already applied to this workspace, and `za project add <repo-url>`, which registers a root-module Go project as a submodule and creates its private context.
- Until a `za` subcommand covers a task (project removal or synchronization, checking drift, creating or removing worktrees), perform it with the native tools below, following `policy.md`.

## Native tools

Native tools are used directly; their behavior is never emulated by hand.

| Tool | Role in this workspace |
|---|---|
| `git` | Repository, submodule (`.gitmodules`, gitlinks) and worktree mechanism. |
| `go` | Go toolchain. Owns root `go.work` and `go.work.sum`; change membership with `go work use`. |

## Integration constraints

Facts that affect reproducibility, kept only for the enabled capabilities:

- A successful workspace build never proves standalone operation. When isolation cannot be established, validate in an external standalone checkout.
- Go: standalone checks in a task worktree set `GOWORK=off`; otherwise Go discovers the root `go.work` by walking parent directories. Root `go.work` references canonical checkouts only and never task worktrees.

## Conventions

- Run commands directly with explicit arguments and working directories.
- Prefer project-owned entry points (scripts, Make/Task targets, CI-equivalent commands) documented in project `tools.md` over reconstructed command lines.
- Every documented command states its mode: `standalone` or `workspace`.
- Capabilities a project requires (an OpenSpec CLI when OpenSpec is adopted, agent skills, plugins) are listed in its `tools.md`.

## Project context templates

`templates/project/` is the single scaffold source for new project contexts. Placeholders state who supplies each value:

| Placeholder | Supplied by |
|---|---|
| `<project-id>`, `<full-submodule-SHA>`, `YYYY-MM-DD` | Structure: known when the project is added. |
| `<discover: ...>` | Inspection of the project repository and its declared authorities. |
| `<decide: ...>` | A human decision (summary, constraints, decisions, plans). |

Never replace a placeholder with an invented fact. Use `not applicable` when a row does not apply.
